// @C113 — two same-key `index` collections are refused.
//
// @EXPECT_ERROR: are both 'index<E1[k]>' in the same structure
//
// Two `index` fields over the same element type AND the same key in one structure
// are refused at compile time (loft#902).
//
// Every other collection kind keeps its own storage, so two of them over one element
// type are two routes to a shared record set — the linked collection group loft#843
// builds. An `index` cannot be: a red-black tree keeps its links in FIELDS OF THE
// ELEMENT RECORD, and that `#left_N / #right_N / #color_N` triple is allocated per
// index TYPE. Two fields whose declared type is identical resolve to that one type,
// so they name one set of links — not two trees, but ONE tree reached through two
// roots.
//
// That is why the FILL looked right and only removal fell over: both roots walked
// the same structure, so lengths and iteration agreed (`a 4 [1234] b 4 [1234]`), and
// the first removal rebalanced through one root and left the other stale — then
// `Child of single-child node should be red`, a panic in `src/tree.rs`, on the next
// walk. Identical on both backends and on the published 2026.8.0.
//
// It is refused rather than made to work because there is nothing to make work: a
// second index with the SAME key answers exactly what the first answers, in the same
// order. The construct's only reachable states were "indistinguishable from one
// index" and "panic".
//
// The scope this file does NOT refuse is pinned by 902-duplicate-index-allowed.loft,
// which must stay green beside it: a different KEY is a different index type with its
// own link triple, two indexes in different structs hold different records, and a
// second route of a different KIND is the workaround the error names.

struct E1 { k: integer, n: text }

struct TwoIndexes { by_k: index<E1[k]>, also_by_k: index<E1[k]> }

fn main() {
  x = TwoIndexes { by_k: [], also_by_k: [] };
  x.by_k = [E1{k:1,n:"alpha"}, E1{k:2,n:"beta"}];
  x.by_k[1] = null;
  println("unreachable {len(x.by_k)}");
}
